!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/32/ltr8/http/meta-http-2.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta-kernel.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta-kernel.tn"
@doc:"""
  Annotation types for describing an HTTP API. No type constructors: nothing here carries the ~
  marker, and an operation is an ordinary `top &` entry in the schema that describes it.

  Governed by the meta-kernel because it has to be. A schema is a meta-schema only if its own !!meta
  is the kernel -- there is no three-level chain -- so a layer above meta.tn is refused with
  'is named as the !!meta of another schema but is not a meta-schema'.

  The annotation TYPES have to live here rather than in the describing schema, and that is the whole
  reason this file exists. An annotation's value is bound through the type its name refers to,
  looked up in the GOVERNING META-SCHEMA's namespace: a locally declared annotation type resolves,
  and its values are then silently dropped. @doc keeps its value because doc is meta-kernel's;
  @method would not keep POST if method were declared beside the operation. See sketch/README.md.
  """
{
  http_method => !enum [GET POST PUT PATCH DELETE HEAD OPTIONS]

  @doc:"Refined, so 42 is not a status."
  status_code => !integer ^ { min: 100  max: 599 }

  parameter_location => !enum [PATH QUERY HEADER]

  @doc:"The HTTP method an operation answers."
  method => @annotation http_method

  @doc:"The path template an operation is served at; a braced segment names a PATH parameter."
  path => @annotation text

  @doc:"Marks a field as a response, and gives its status. The field's type is the response body."
  status => @annotation status_code

  @doc:"Marks a field as a parameter, and says where it is carried. The field's type is its type."
  parameter => @annotation parameter_location
}
